# Local Runner Safety

- `tools/trainingpeaks-export` operates around real TrainingPeaks data and local browser state. Treat all changes here as high-risk.
- Preserve the prepare -> validate -> execute pattern when touching runner flows, action pipelines, or local automation.
- Dry-run must remain the default unless the task explicitly changes that contract with approval gates.
- Do not introduce real TrainingPeaks mutation without an explicit approval step and a clear operator signal that execution is live.
- Never log auth headers, cookies, bearer tokens, session material, or private athlete data to console, files, debug exports, or docs.
- Changes to LaunchAgent files, schedule wrappers, or local automation entrypoints require explicit review because they can create unattended behavior.
- Any script that touches TrainingPeaks APIs, Playwright state, or the persistent local browser profile is high-risk and should be audited before implementation.
